IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sssa-nouns`
IMPORT `sssa-part1-preliminary`
IMPORT `sssa-part2-scheme`
IMPORT `sssa-part3-administration`
IMPORT `sssa-part4-miscellaneous`

-- Silver Support Scheme Act 2015 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal
-- consolidation in force from 1 December 2025 -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a person who is, or may become, entitled to Silver Support payments (a
-- citizen of Singapore aged 65 or over, or about to be).  This layer phrases the
-- rules already encoded in the modules imported above as the questions that
-- person would ask: am I eligible, how much and how will I be paid, what may the
-- authorities do with my information and can I stop it, what must I repay, what
-- can I be made to tell the authorities, and what are the offences and
-- penalties.  Nothing here is new law.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS.  Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, a number, a date,
-- or a choice from a list -- one for each fact the person can state, each with an
-- @desc worded as the person would be asked.  The records and MAYBE inputs the
-- long modules expect are built inside each question, in its WHERE, from those
-- answers, and the SAME module rule is then called; no rule is restated here.
--   * A fact the person may not know is asked as "Yes / No / I am not sure"
--     (`My answer`); "I am not sure" becomes NOTHING, and a rule that cannot
--     answer without it answers NOTHING.
--   * A birth year, month or day, or an amount, that the person does not know is
--     asked as 0, and becomes NOTHING.
--   * The prescribed criteria, benefits, amounts and manner are in regulations
--     that are not among the sources.  The Act's own figures (the ceilings of its
--     penalties, the $1,000 cap on a compounded sum) are taken from the modules.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Act itself
-- gives; NOTHING means the Act does not answer on these facts (see NOTES.md,
-- "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").  Never read NOTHING as no.
--
-- A question is asked of a CITIZEN-INDIVIDUAL's own situation.  There is no seat
-- for an official: where a provision addresses only an official (ss 5, 8(1), (2),
-- (5), 9(1), (3), (4), (6), 18), the rule is in layer 1 and the person meets it
-- only through the questions below.

DECLARE `My answer` IS ONE OF
    Yes
    No
    `I am not sure`

-- A change in the person's circumstances, for the two questions on which the Act is silent.
DECLARE `What has changed for me` IS ONE OF
    `I left Singapore`
    `I stopped being a citizen of Singapore`
    `My income or assets changed`
    `Something else changed`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Wiring: the person's answers become the modules' inputs.  Not questions.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- A birth date from what the person knows: 0 means not known.
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      month IS A NUMBER
      day IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Birth facts`
`my birth from what I know` MEANS
    `Birth facts` WITH
        `year of birth` IS IF year EQUALS 0 THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST year -- input mapping
        `month of birth` IS IF month EQUALS 0 THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST month -- input mapping
        `day of birth` IS IF day EQUALS 0 THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST day -- input mapping

-- An answer of Yes, No or "I am not sure" as a MAYBE BOOLEAN.
GIVEN answer IS A `My answer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`what I say, as a fact` MEANS
    CONSIDER answer
    WHEN Yes THEN JUST TRUE -- input mapping
    WHEN No THEN JUST FALSE -- input mapping
    WHEN `I am not sure` THEN NOTHING -- input mapping

-- An amount that the person gives as 0 when they do not know it.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`my amount if I know it` MEANS
    IF amount EQUALS 0 THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST amount -- input mapping

§ `The Silver Support Scheme Act 2015 -- my questions`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Am I eligible for Silver Support? (ss 6 and 7)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 6(2).  "Attains 65 years of age" is counted on the 65th anniversary of the
-- date of birth; a person born on 29 February reaches 65 on 1 March; where the
-- day cannot be ascertained the 1st is taken, and where the month cannot be
-- ascertained, January.  Nothing can be worked out without the year of birth.
@export On what date do I reach 65 years of age for Silver Support (s 6(2))?
GIVEN `my year of birth` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year were you born? (0 if you do not know)
      `my month of birth` IS A NUMBER @desc In which month were you born, from 1 for January to 12 for December? (0 if you do not know)
      `my day of birth` IS A NUMBER @desc On which day of the month were you born? (0 if you do not know)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what date do I reach 65` IS
    `s 6(2)(a) the date on which the individual attains 65 years of age` (`my birth from what I know` `my year of birth` `my month of birth` `my day of birth`)

-- s 6(1)(b) with s 6(2).  The Act does not say as at when the question is asked,
-- so you give the date you are asking about.
@export Have I reached 65 years of age for Silver Support (s 6(1)(b))?
GIVEN `my year of birth` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year were you born? (0 if you do not know)
      `my month of birth` IS A NUMBER @desc In which month were you born, from 1 for January to 12 for December? (0 if you do not know)
      `my day of birth` IS A NUMBER @desc On which day of the month were you born? (0 if you do not know)
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking whether you have reached 65?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I reached 65` IS
    `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`my birth from what I know` `my year of birth` `my month of birth` `my day of birth`) `the date I am asking about`

-- s 6(1).  An eligible individual is a citizen of Singapore, aged 65 or over, who
-- satisfies all the other eligibility criteria that may be prescribed.  The
-- prescribed criteria are in regulations; you say whether you meet them.
@export Am I an eligible individual for Silver Support (s 6(1))?
GIVEN `I am a citizen of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a citizen of Singapore?
      `my year of birth` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year were you born? (0 if you do not know)
      `my month of birth` IS A NUMBER @desc In which month were you born, from 1 for January to 12 for December? (0 if you do not know)
      `my day of birth` IS A NUMBER @desc On which day of the month were you born? (0 if you do not know)
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking whether you are an eligible individual?
      `I meet the other criteria` IS A `My answer` @desc Do you satisfy all the other eligibility criteria that the regulations prescribe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an eligible individual` IS
    `s 6(1) the individual is an eligible individual` `I am a citizen of Singapore` (`my birth from what I know` `my year of birth` `my month of birth` `my day of birth`) `the date I am asking about` (`what I say, as a fact` `I meet the other criteria`)

-- s 7(1).  An eligible individual is eligible to receive the benefits that may be
-- prescribed.  A person who is not an eligible individual is outside this grant;
-- the section does not say that such a person receives nothing.
@export Am I eligible to receive Silver Support benefits (s 7(1))?
GIVEN `I am a citizen of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a citizen of Singapore?
      `my year of birth` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year were you born? (0 if you do not know)
      `my month of birth` IS A NUMBER @desc In which month were you born, from 1 for January to 12 for December? (0 if you do not know)
      `my day of birth` IS A NUMBER @desc On which day of the month were you born? (0 if you do not know)
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking whether you are eligible to receive benefits?
      `I meet the other criteria` IS A `My answer` @desc Do you satisfy all the other eligibility criteria that the regulations prescribe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I eligible to receive benefits` IS
    `s 7(1) the individual is eligible to receive the benefits that may be prescribed` (`s 6(1) the individual is an eligible individual` `I am a citizen of Singapore` (`my birth from what I know` `my year of birth` `my month of birth` `my day of birth`) `the date I am asking about` (`what I say, as a fact` `I meet the other criteria`))

-- s 7(1) and (2).  The amount is prescribed for the class you are in; it is in the
-- regulations, so you give it.  The Act itself fixes no amount.
@export How much Silver Support benefit am I eligible to receive, in dollars (s 7(1) and (2))?
GIVEN `I am a citizen of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a citizen of Singapore?
      `my year of birth` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year were you born? (0 if you do not know)
      `my month of birth` IS A NUMBER @desc In which month were you born, from 1 for January to 12 for December? (0 if you do not know)
      `my day of birth` IS A NUMBER @desc On which day of the month were you born? (0 if you do not know)
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking?
      `I meet the other criteria` IS A `My answer` @desc Do you satisfy all the other eligibility criteria that the regulations prescribe?
      `the amount the regulations prescribe for my class` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount, in dollars, do the regulations prescribe for your class of eligible individual? (0 if you do not know)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much am I eligible to receive` IS
    `s 7(1) the amount of benefit an eligible individual is eligible to receive` (`s 6(1) the individual is an eligible individual` `I am a citizen of Singapore` (`my birth from what I know` `my year of birth` `my month of birth` `my day of birth`) `the date I am asking about` (`what I say, as a fact` `I meet the other criteria`)) (`my amount if I know it` `the amount the regulations prescribe for my class`)

-- s 7(1).  "In such manner ... as may be prescribed": how and when the benefit is
-- paid is in the regulations, which are not among the sources.  The Act does not
-- answer, so this question answers NOTHING for everyone.
@export How and when will my Silver Support benefit be paid (s 7(1))?
GIVEN `I am a citizen of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a citizen of Singapore?
      `my year of birth` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year were you born? (0 if you do not know)
      `my month of birth` IS A NUMBER @desc In which month were you born, from 1 for January to 12 for December? (0 if you do not know)
      `my day of birth` IS A NUMBER @desc On which day of the month were you born? (0 if you do not know)
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking?
      `I meet the other criteria` IS A `My answer` @desc Do you satisfy all the other eligibility criteria that the regulations prescribe?
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
DECIDE `How and when will I be paid` IS
    `s 7(1) the manner in which an eligible individual is to receive the benefit` (`s 6(1) the individual is an eligible individual` `I am a citizen of Singapore` (`my birth from what I know` `my year of birth` `my month of birth` `my day of birth`) `the date I am asking about` (`what I say, as a fact` `I meet the other criteria`))
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the manner (and so the timing) of payment is "such manner ... as may be prescribed" and the regulations are not among the sources
        NOTHING

-- When the benefit stops or is withdrawn.  The Act has no provision that ends,
-- suspends or withdraws a benefit, so this question answers NOTHING whatever has
-- changed.  (If the person has stopped being a citizen, s 6(1)(a) is no longer met
-- and s 10(1)(a)(i) treats a payment to a person who is not an eligible
-- individual as recoverable; that is the question on repayment below, not an
-- answer to whether the benefit "stops".)
@export Does the Act say that my Silver Support benefit stops or is withdrawn because of this change (ss 6, 7, 20(2)(c))?
GIVEN `what has changed` IS A `What has changed for me` @desc What has changed for you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my benefit stop because of the change` IS
    CONSIDER `what has changed`
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no provision of the Act ends, suspends or withdraws a benefit, and the terms and conditions of each benefit are for regulations (s 20(2)(c)), which are not among the sources
    WHEN `I left Singapore` THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no provision of the Act ends, suspends or withdraws a benefit, and the terms and conditions of each benefit are for regulations (s 20(2)(c)), which are not among the sources
    WHEN `I stopped being a citizen of Singapore` THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no provision of the Act ends, suspends or withdraws a benefit, and the terms and conditions of each benefit are for regulations (s 20(2)(c)), which are not among the sources
    WHEN `My income or assets changed` THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no provision of the Act ends, suspends or withdraws a benefit, and the terms and conditions of each benefit are for regulations (s 20(2)(c)), which are not among the sources
    WHEN `Something else changed` THEN NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `What the authorities may do with my information (ss 8 and 9)`
-- Situation: asked only of a person whose information has been, or may be, obtained from a department under a Minister's direction.
-- The form can ask "Has your information been shared with the Commissioner, the Board or an administrator?" before showing this group.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 8(3).  If you opt out of the sharing of your means information, then from the
-- time the authorised person is told, they must not look at the information they
-- got or use or share what they had already looked at, unless you consent.
@export Is the authorised person barred from accessing or using my means information because I opted out (s 8(3))?
GIVEN `what the authorised person did` IS AN `Act on means information` @desc What did the authorised person do with your means information?
      `I opted out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you opt out, in the manner the Commissioner determined, of the sharing of your means information?
      `the authorised person was told` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the authorised person been told that you opted out?
      `I consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you consented to the authorised person's access or use?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the authorised person barred` IS
    `s 8(3) the authorised person is barred from the act` `what the authorised person did` `I opted out` `the authorised person was told` `I consented`

-- s 8(4)(a).  A person who discloses information as the Minister directed is not
-- guilty of an offence and incurs no civil liability merely by doing so, subject
-- to s 8(3).
@export Is a department protected from liability to me for passing on my information as the Minister directed (s 8(4)(a))?
GIVEN `it passed on information as a Minister's direction required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the department or authority pass on the information in accordance with a direction of the Minister under section 8(1)(a) or 8(2)(a)?
      `my opt-out barred it` IS A `My answer` @desc Was the disclosure an act that your opt-out barred under section 8(3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the department protected from liability to me` IS
    `s 8(4)(a) the person is not guilty or liable merely by disclosing in accordance with the direction` `it passed on information as a Minister's direction required` (`what I say, as a fact` `my opt-out barred it`)

-- s 8(6).  Doing an act in contravention of s 8(3) is an offence.
@export Is it an offence to do something to my information that my opt-out barred (s 8(6))?
GIVEN `the act contravened my opt-out under section 8(3)` IS A `My answer` @desc Did the act contravene your opt-out under section 8(3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is breaching my opt-out an offence` IS
    `s 8(6) the person is guilty of an offence` (`what I say, as a fact` `the act contravened my opt-out under section 8(3)`)

-- s 9(2).  Without your consent, information obtained under s 8 may be used or
-- disclosed only if the purpose is to communicate or manage it as part of the
-- administration or enforcement of the Act or the administration of the Scheme.
@export Is it authorised to use or disclose my information without my consent for this purpose (s 9(2))?
GIVEN `the information was obtained under section 8` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the information obtained under section 8(1) (means information) or section 8(2) (other confidential information)?
      `I have consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you consented to this use or disclosure?
      `to administer or enforce the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose to communicate or manage the information as part of the administration or enforcement of the Act?
      `to administer the Scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose to communicate or manage the information as part of the administration of the Scheme?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it authorised to use or disclose my information` IS
    `s 9(2) the use or disclosure is authorised` `the use or disclosure`
    WHERE
        `the use or disclosure` MEANS `Use or disclosure asked about under section 9(2)` WITH
            `is of means information obtained under section 8(1) or of confidential information other than means information obtained under section 8(2)` IS `the information was obtained under section 8`
            `is without the consent of the individual to whom the information relates` IS NOT `I have consented`
            `has the purpose of communicating or managing the information as part of the administration or enforcement of this Act` IS `to administer or enforce the Act`
            `has the purpose of communicating or managing the information as part of the administration of the Scheme` IS `to administer the Scheme`

-- s 9(5).  If you opt out of a report about you for a public scheme, then from
-- the time the Commissioner, the Board or an administrator is told, they must not
-- give such a report, unless you consent.
@export Must a report about me for a public scheme stop because I opted out (s 9(5))?
GIVEN `who would give the report` IS A Capacity @desc Who would give the report: the Commissioner, the Board, an administrator, or someone else?
      `it is such a report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a report stating whether you satisfy the eligibility criteria for any benefit under the Scheme and the description and amount of each benefit you are eligible to receive or have received (section 9(3)(b))?
      `I opted out of the report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you opt out, in the manner the Commissioner determined, of a report about you?
      `they were told` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the Commissioner, the Board or the administrator been told that you opted out?
      `I consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you consented to the report?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the report about me stop` IS
    `s 9(5) the provider is barred from providing the report` `who would give the report` `it is such a report` `I opted out of the report` `they were told` `I consented`

-- s 9(7).  Any act in contravention of s 9(2), (3) or (5) is an offence.
@export Is it an offence to use or pass on my information against the rules in section 9 (s 9(7))?
GIVEN `it contravened section 9(2)` IS A `My answer` @desc Did the act contravene section 9(2) (use or disclosure without your consent for a purpose that section does not allow)?
      `it contravened section 9(3)` IS A `My answer` @desc Did the act contravene section 9(3) (giving a report for a public scheme otherwise than as that section allows)?
      `it contravened section 9(5)` IS A `My answer` @desc Did the act contravene section 9(5) (giving a report after you opted out)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it an offence to breach section 9` IS
    `s 9(7) the person is guilty of an offence` (`what I say, as a fact` `it contravened section 9(2)`) (`what I say, as a fact` `it contravened section 9(3)`) (`what I say, as a fact` `it contravened section 9(5)`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `If I have been paid too much or not entitled (s 10)`
-- Situation: asked only of a person who has been paid a cash grant or other benefit and told, or fears, that some of it must be repaid.
-- The form can ask "Have you been told you must pay money back?" before showing this group.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 10(1).  If a benefit is paid as a cash grant and the recipient is not an
-- eligible individual, or is not eligible for that cash grant, the amount paid is
-- recoverable as a debt due to the Government; if the amount paid is more than the
-- recipient is eligible to receive, the excess is.
@export How much of a cash grant must I pay back because it was paid in error (s 10(1))?
GIVEN `it was paid as a cash grant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the benefit paid to you as a cash grant?
      `I was an eligible individual` IS A `My answer` @desc Were you an eligible individual when it was paid?
      `I was eligible for that cash grant` IS A `My answer` @desc Were you eligible for that cash grant?
      `the amount I was paid` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in dollars, were you paid?
      `the amount I was eligible to receive` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in dollars, were you eligible to receive by way of that cash grant? (0 if you do not know)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much must I pay back` IS
    `s 10(1) the amount made recoverable as a debt due to the Government` `it was paid as a cash grant` (`what I say, as a fact` `I was an eligible individual`) (`what I say, as a fact` `I was eligible for that cash grant`) `the amount I was paid` (`my amount if I know it` `the amount I was eligible to receive`)

-- s 10(2).  Anyone, eligible or not, who obtains a cash grant or other benefit by a
-- false or misleading statement made knowingly or recklessly, or by a document
-- known (or that ought reasonably to be known) to be false in a material
-- particular, must pay back the amount so obtained.
@export How much must I pay back because I got a benefit by a false statement or document (s 10(2))?
GIVEN `I knowingly or recklessly made a false or misleading statement to get it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you obtain the cash grant or other benefit by making a false or misleading statement, knowingly or recklessly?
      `I used a document I knew or ought to have known was false to get it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you obtain it by producing or providing, or causing to be produced or provided, a document that you knew, or ought reasonably to have known, was false in a material particular?
      `the amount I obtained` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in dollars, was the cash grant or other benefit you obtained?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much must I pay back for a false statement` IS
    `s 10(2) the amount made recoverable as a debt due to the Government` `I knowingly or recklessly made a false or misleading statement to get it` `I used a document I knew or ought to have known was false to get it` `the amount I obtained`

-- s 10(3).  An administrator may recover, for the Government, an amount due under
-- s 10(1) or (2), by set-off or otherwise, from a cash grant or other benefit you
-- are eligible to receive and from any other sum the administrator owes you.
@export Can the administrator take what I owe out of what I am owed (s 10(3))?
GIVEN `the one recovering is an administrator` IS A `My answer` @desc Is the body recovering the money an administrator of the Scheme?
      `I owe an amount under section 10` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an amount due from you to the Government under section 10(1) or 10(2)?
      `where the money would come from` IS A `Source of recovery` @desc Where would the money be taken from?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the administrator take it out of what I am owed` IS
    `s 10(3) the administrator may recover the amount from the source` (`what I say, as a fact` `the one recovering is an administrator`) `I owe an amount under section 10` `where the money would come from`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Offences, penalties and what I can be made to pay (ss 11 to 17)`
-- Situation: asked only of a person who has been asked for information or documents, accused of an offence under the Act, or asked to pay a sum to settle one.
-- The form can ask "Have you been asked for information, or accused of breaking this Act?" before showing this group.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 11(1).
@export Have I committed the offence of obtaining a benefit by a false statement or document (s 11(1))?
GIVEN `I knowingly or recklessly made a false or misleading statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly or recklessly make a false or misleading statement?
      `I produced or provided a document I knew or ought to have known was false` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you produce or provide, or cause to be produced or provided, a document that you knew, or ought reasonably to have known, was false in a material particular?
      `I dishonestly obtained a benefit by it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you, intending to dishonestly induce another person to accept the statement or document as genuine, dishonestly obtain a cash grant or other benefit under the Scheme?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed the offence of a false statement` IS
    `s 11(1) the person is guilty of an offence` `I knowingly or recklessly made a false or misleading statement` `I produced or provided a document I knew or ought to have known was false` `I dishonestly obtained a benefit by it`

-- s 12.
@export Can the court order me to repay when I am convicted of an offence in connection with a benefit (s 12)?
GIVEN `I received a cash grant or other benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you received a cash grant or other benefit under the Scheme?
      `I was convicted in connection with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been convicted of an offence under the Act in connection with that cash grant or benefit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the court order me to repay on conviction` IS
    `s 12 the court may order the person to pay the certified amount to an administrator` `I received a cash grant or other benefit` `I was convicted in connection with it`

-- s 13.
@export Is the administrator's certificate evidence of what I received or owe (s 13)?
GIVEN `it purports to be issued by an administrator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate purport to be issued by an administrator?
      `it certifies what I received` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it certify the amount of a cash grant or other benefit you received as at a date?
      `it certifies what I owe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it certify the amount recoverable from you as at a date in respect of a cash grant or other benefit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the certificate evidence of what I received or owe` IS
    `s 13 the certificate is prima facie evidence of the amount stated` `it purports to be issued by an administrator` `it certifies what I received` `it certifies what I owe`

-- s 14(1).
@export Can the Commissioner or an investigator require me to give information or documents (s 14(1))?
GIVEN `who is asking me` IS A `Person requiring` @desc Who is asking you: the Commissioner, an investigator, or someone else?
      `why they want it` IS A `Purpose of the requirement` @desc For what purpose do they say they want it?
      `what they ask me to do` IS A `Thing required` @desc What are you asked to do?
      `I was given written notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you given a written notice? (this matters when you are asked to attend or answer questions)
      `the time and place are reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the time and place they specified reasonable? (this matters when you are asked to attend or answer questions)
      `it concerns the Scheme's benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the questions or the statement concern the disbursement or conferment of a benefit under the Scheme?
      `they believe it is connected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they believe, on reasonable grounds, that the information, document or record is connected with the disbursement or conferment of a benefit under the Scheme?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be required to give information` IS
    `s 14(1) the requirer may make the requirement` `who is asking me` `why they want it` `what they ask me to do` `I was given written notice` `the time and place are reasonable` `it concerns the Scheme's benefits` `they believe it is connected`

-- What I must tell the authorities.  No provision of the deposited body of the Act
-- requires a recipient to report a change of circumstances: the word "report"
-- occurs only for reports the authorities make about the person (s 9(3)(b), s 9(5)).
-- The person's duties to give information are the compulsory powers of s 14, asked
-- above, and the terms and conditions of each benefit are for regulations (s 20(2)(c)).
@export Does the Act require me to tell the authorities about this change (ss 14, 20(2)(c))?
GIVEN `what has changed` IS A `What has changed for me` @desc What has changed for you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I tell the authorities about the change` IS
    CONSIDER `what has changed`
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no provision of the Act requires a recipient to report a change of circumstances, and the terms and conditions of each benefit are for regulations (s 20(2)(c)), which are not among the sources
    WHEN `I left Singapore` THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no provision of the Act requires a recipient to report a change of circumstances, and the terms and conditions of each benefit are for regulations (s 20(2)(c)), which are not among the sources
    WHEN `I stopped being a citizen of Singapore` THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no provision of the Act requires a recipient to report a change of circumstances, and the terms and conditions of each benefit are for regulations (s 20(2)(c)), which are not among the sources
    WHEN `My income or assets changed` THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no provision of the Act requires a recipient to report a change of circumstances, and the terms and conditions of each benefit are for regulations (s 20(2)(c)), which are not among the sources
    WHEN `Something else changed` THEN NOTHING

-- s 14(4).  The count of days is from the requirement to the day you provided or
-- produced it, or to the day you are asking about if you have not.
@export Have I committed an offence by not giving the information or documents in time (s 14(4))?
GIVEN `who required it` IS A `Person requiring` @desc Who required you to provide the information or produce the document or record: the Commissioner, an investigator, or someone else?
      `it was required under section 14(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you required to provide information or to produce a document or record for inspection (not merely to attend)?
      `I refused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you refuse?
      `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days did they allow you?
      `the days counted` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days have passed from the requirement to the day you provided or produced it, or to today if you have not?
      `I have a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a reasonable excuse?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed an offence by not giving it in time` IS
    `s 14(4) the person is guilty of an offence` `who required it` `it was required under section 14(1)(b)` `I refused` `the days allowed` `the days counted` `I have a reasonable excuse`

-- s 15.
@export Have I committed an offence by obstructing the Commissioner or an investigator (s 15)?
GIVEN `who I obstructed` IS A `Person requiring` @desc Whom did you obstruct, hinder or impede: the Commissioner, an investigator, or someone else?
      `I obstructed them in their duties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you obstruct, hinder or impede them in the performance or execution of a duty, or of anything they are authorised, empowered or required to do under the Act?
      `I have a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a reasonable excuse?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed an offence by obstructing` IS
    `s 15 the person is guilty of an offence` `who I obstructed` `I obstructed them in their duties` `I have a reasonable excuse`

-- ss 8(6), 9(7), 11(1), 14(4) and 15.  The most a court may impose.
@export What is the heaviest sentence a court may impose for this offence (ss 8(6), 9(7), 11(1), 14(4) and 15)?
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence under the Act` @desc Which offence are you asking about?
GIVETH A Penalty
DECIDE `What is the heaviest sentence for the offence` IS
    `ss 8(6), 9(7), 11(1), 14(4) and 15 the greatest penalty for the offence` `the offence`

-- s 16(1).
@export As an officer of a body corporate that committed an offence, am I guilty of it too (s 16(1))?
GIVEN `the kind of body` IS A `Kind of entity` @desc What kind of body committed the offence?
      `the offence is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it proved that the body committed an offence under the Act?
      `my position` IS A `Position in a body corporate` @desc What was your position in the body corporate?
      `I consented or connived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it proved that the offence was committed with your consent or connivance?
      `it is due to my neglect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it proved that the offence is attributable to neglect on your part?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of the body corporate's offence` IS
    `s 16(1) the officer is guilty of the offence as well as the body corporate` `the kind of body` `the offence is proved` `my position` `I consented or connived` `it is due to my neglect`

-- s 16(2).
@export If the affairs of a body corporate are managed by its members, am I treated as a director (s 16(2))?
GIVEN `its affairs are managed by its members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the affairs of the body corporate managed by its members?
      `it was my act or default in managing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it your act or default in connection with your functions of management?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as a director` IS
    `s 16(2) section 16(1) applies to the member as if the member were a director` `its affairs are managed by its members` `it was my act or default in managing`

-- s 16(3).
@export As a partner in a partnership that committed an offence, am I guilty of it too (s 16(3))?
GIVEN `the kind of body` IS A `Kind of entity` @desc What kind of body committed the offence?
      `the offence is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it proved that the partnership committed an offence under the Act?
      `I am a partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a partner?
      `I purported to act as a partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you purport to act as a partner?
      `I consented or connived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it proved that the offence was committed with your consent or connivance?
      `it is due to my neglect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it proved that the offence is attributable to neglect on your part?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of the partnership's offence` IS
    `s 16(3) the partner is guilty of the offence as well as the partnership` `the kind of body` `the offence is proved` (`s 16(5) the person is a partner` `I am a partner` `I purported to act as a partner`) `I consented or connived` `it is due to my neglect`

-- s 16(4).
@export As an officer or member of an unincorporated association that committed an offence, am I guilty of it too (s 16(4))?
GIVEN `the kind of body` IS A `Kind of entity` @desc What kind of body committed the offence?
      `the offence is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it proved that the association committed an offence under the Act?
      `my position` IS A `Position in an unincorporated association` @desc What was your position in the association?
      `I am a member of its governing body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of its governing body?
      `I consented or connived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it proved that the offence was committed with your consent or connivance?
      `it is due to my neglect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it proved that the offence is attributable to neglect on your part?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of the association's offence` IS
    `s 16(4) the officer or member is guilty of the offence as well as the unincorporated association` `the kind of body` `the offence is proved` (`s 16(5)(b) the person is an officer of an unincorporated association` `my position`) `I am a member of its governing body` `I consented or connived` `it is due to my neglect`

-- s 17(1).  The Board (here fixed as the compounding body: the Act's own) may
-- compound an offence that is prescribed as compoundable, by collecting from a
-- person reasonably suspected of it a sum not exceeding the lower of one half of
-- the maximum fine and $1,000.  The Board is the compounder asked about, so it is
-- not a fact the person states.
@export If I am asked to pay a sum to settle an offence, what is the most I can be asked for, in dollars (s 17(1))?
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence under the Act` @desc Which offence are you suspected of?
      `it is a compoundable offence` IS A `My answer` @desc Have the regulations prescribed this offence as one that may be compounded?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be asked to pay to settle` IS
    -- Placeholders: the compounder is the Board (the Act's own compounding body) and the person asking is the person reasonably suspected of the offence (the question's premise); neither is a fact the person states.
    IF `s 17(1) the Board or its authorised officer or employee may compound the offence` `the Board` (`what I say, as a fact` `it is a compoundable offence`) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 17(1) the greatest sum that may be collected` `the greatest fine for the offence`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): which offences are "prescribed as a compoundable offence" is in regulations that are not among the sources
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the penalty for the offence` MEANS `ss 8(6), 9(7), 11(1), 14(4) and 15 the greatest penalty for the offence` `the offence`
        `the greatest fine for the offence` MEANS `the penalty for the offence`'s `greatest fine in dollars`

-- s 17(2).
@export After I pay the sum to settle an offence, can I still be prosecuted for it (s 17(2))?
GIVEN `I have paid the sum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you paid the sum of money?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are further proceedings barred once I have paid` IS
    `s 17(2) no further proceedings are to be taken against the person in respect of the offence` `I have paid the sum`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Can I hold an official personally liable? (s 19)`
-- Situation: asked only of a person who wants to know whether an official can be held personally liable for something done under the Act.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 19(1) to (3).  JUST TRUE means: no liability lies personally against that
-- official.
@export Is this official protected from personal liability to me for what they did under the Act (s 19)?
GIVEN `the official` IS A Capacity @desc Who is the official?
      `they acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the official act in good faith?
      `they acted with reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the official act with reasonable care?
      `it was in executing the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was what they did or failed to do in the execution, or purported execution, of the Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the official protected from personal liability` IS
    `s 19 no liability lies personally against the individual` `the official` `they acted in good faith` `they acted with reasonable care` `it was in executing the Act`

-- s 19(4).  "To avoid doubt, this section does not exclude any liability under
-- section 20 of the Financial Procedure Act 1966 or under section 8(6) or 9(7)."
@export Does the protection from personal liability leave this liability in place (s 19(4))?
GIVEN `the liability` IS A `Kind of liability` @desc Which liability are you asking about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 19 leave the liability in place` IS
    `s 19(4) section 19 leaves the liability in place` `the liability`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `What the regulations may cover (s 20)`
-- Situation: asked of anyone who wants to know what the regulations may deal with, for example when payment stops or whether an assessment can be reviewed.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 20(2).  The Act leaves to regulations the benefits and amounts, the method and
-- manner of paying, the terms and conditions (which is where payment stopping or
-- being withdrawn would be dealt with), the assessment of eligibility, the review
-- of an assessment and its time limit, and fees.  This question says whether the
-- Minister may make regulations on the matter; it does not say what they provide.
@export Can the Minister make regulations on this matter that affects me (s 20(2))?
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `Matter for regulations` @desc Which matter are you asking about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can regulations deal with the matter` IS
    `s 20(2) the Minister may make regulations for or with respect to the matter` `the matter`
